<title>CANADA: ASA selects Canadair jets.</title>
<headline>ASA selects Canadair jets.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlantic Southeast Airlines said Tuesday it intended to acquire 30 Canadair regional jets plus options for an additional 60 Canadair jets.</p>
<p>A definitive agreement confirming the purchase is expected to be concluded shortly, it said.</p>
<p>The sale will be the largest single Canadair jet transaction to date. Value of the 30 firm aircraft, including spares provisioning, would be about US$600 million.</p>
<p>Deliveries will begin in August this year at a rate of one a month. Canadair is part of Bombardier Inc.</p>
</text>
